.th DJ IV 5/27/74
.sh NAME
dj \*- DJ-11 communications multiplexer
.sh DESCRIPTION
Each line attached to the DJ-11 communications multiplexer
behaves as described in
.it tty
(IV).
Input and output for each line may independently
be set to run at any of 16 speeds in groups of four
(by means of hardware straps);
see
.it tty
(IV)
for the encoding.
Speeds cannot be changed by software.
Parity is ignored internally.
.sh FILES
/dev/tty[a-p]
.sh "SEE ALSO"
tty (IV), stty (II)
.sh AUTHOR
Ian Johnstone (University of New South Wales)
